+## NoCpuPartner (2026-11-15, default on)
+3-cab test 2026-11-15 02:18 PT: a Teamplay duo vs a solo cabinet. The duo cleared the results screen; the solo, whose
+partner was a game-made CPU, hung until TEST. Every hang so far had a cabinet with a CPU partner; Fes 1on1 (no partner),
+4-human rooms and Teamplay duos clear. The game seats CPUs itself (they never appear on the network) and gives a CPU
+partner to every solo without a human teammate, so the only server-side lever is which rooms are formed.
+
+With `OnlineMatching.NoCpuPartner` (true by default in the config; the `Matchmaker` class property defaults to false):
+* 2v2-rule worlds (everything except `OneOnOneWorlds` and the pair worlds 5/21/22) form **only full 4-human rooms**:
+  4 solos (2 + 2), a Teamplay duo + 2 solos (the solos are teammates), or duo vs duo.
+* The fill timer (`FillAfterSeconds` / `FillTimerMode` / `MaxFillWaitSeconds` / in-store overrides) no longer makes
+  short-handed rooms there. 2 or 3 solos, a duo + 1 solo, or a lone duo keep waiting (a 4th human can still join at any
+  time) until the cabinet's own matching timeout (150 s by default), which gets `MATCH_CANCELED`. One `NOCPU hold` log
+  line per waiting unit when the fill timer would have fired.
+* The server can't move a cabinet into Fes 1on1: the mode is the cabinet's choice (world id in its entry) and no reply
+  carries a mode. A 1v1 room in a 2v2 world is exactly the CPU-partner case. Fes 1on1 (`OneOnOneWorlds`, default "20")
+  keeps matching two solos at once, so for two players the answer is to pick Fes 1on1 on both cabinets.
+* `AllowPartialRooms`, `CpuStandInSeats`, `HumansTeamVsCpu` and `LoneTeamVsCpu` are ignored for those worlds.
+* A team entry whose partner is the game's CPU stand-in ("N") already has a CPU partner: it is never placed (one
+  `NOCPU-WARN` line) and waits for its own timeout.
+* `false` = pre-v11 behaviour. Tests: `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/NoCpuPartnerTests.cs`.
+
 ## Results-hang fixes (2026-11-14, exvs2-lobbies `analysis/results-hang-fixes.md` section 4) — fake cabinets only
 All off by default except the log line. Tests: `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/HangFixTests.cs`,
 exvs2-lobbies `server-sketch/loadtest/hangfix_e2e.py`.
